<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand-Bassam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grand-Bassam is a town on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abidjan">Abidjan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> signed treaties with local rulers and built a fort there in 1843, and it served as the first capital of the French colony from 1893 until yellow fever epidemics prompted the move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bingerville">Bingerville</a> in 1900. Its colonial quarter of merchant houses and public buildings was inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2012.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-bassam.jpg" alt="Grand-Bassam" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joker-x http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Joker-x · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:800px-Grand-Bassam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
